# Cabecalhos de seguranca do Netlify (app.pmaxing.pt).
#
# A CSP esta em modo Report-Only: NAO bloqueia nada, so escreve na consola do
# browser o que bloquearia. Usa a app toda uns dias (login com email, Google,
# GitHub e Discord, Focus, Notebook com fotos e anexos, Schedule, Profile com
# avatar, Dashboard) e abre a consola. Se aparecer "[Report Only] Refused to
# ...", acrescenta a origem em falta. Quando estiver limpa, muda o nome do
# cabecalho para Content-Security-Policy (sem Report-Only).
#
# Confirmado no index.html: sem scripts inline e sem Google Fonts.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://*.supabase.co https://lh3.googleusercontent.com https://avatars.githubusercontent.com https://cdn.discordapp.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.pmaxing.pt https://*.supabase.co; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# O service worker e a pagina de entrada nao ficam em cache: senao uma versao
# antiga da app pode continuar a ser servida a quem ja a visitou.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
